From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] 0144: blueline GPU: zap shader through PAS 13 and
 CP_SET_SECURE_MODE 0 before the draw stage (bluegpu=7)

draw1 (bluegpu=7 step 1): CP_BLIT fills complete, every fence (MEM_WRITE,
CACHE_FLUSH_TS, CCU colour/depth flush TS) lands, no SMMU or CP fault, but
no pixel changes. The GPU comes up in secure mode and nothing took it out.

Between stage 4's WHERE_AM_I and the draw stage, as mainline a6xx hw_init
does after a6xx_cp_init (a6xx_zap_shader_init -> zap_shader_load_mdt):

 - image from /blueline-gpu "zap-elf" (tools/mkadt.py --gpu-fw squashes the
   phone's /vendor/firmware a630_zap.mdt + .b00-.b02; Google-signed, not
   committed), checked as mdt_header_valid / qcom_mdt_read_metadata /
   qcom_mdt_get_size / qcom_mdt_load_no_init check it;
 - is_call_available(PIL, AUTH_AND_RESET) (qcom_pas_is_available);
 - PAS INIT_IMAGE(13, meta_pa): x0 0x42000201 x1 0x82, metadata (ELF
   header + phdrs, then the hash segment: 6684 bytes) in a fresh contiguous
   page below 4G made Normal NC (dma_alloc_coherent), leaked;
 - PAS MEM_SETUP(13, 0x8c415000, 0x1000) (relocatable image): x0 0x42000202
   x1 3; region = sdm845.dtsi gpu_mem 0x8c415000 size 0x2000, outside
   XNU's RAM (0xf4000000+);
 - the loadable segment (p_paddr 0x5000, 0x7b0 bytes) to region +
   p_paddr - min(p_paddr) through a Device mapping, read back, dsb;
 - PAS AUTH_AND_RESET(13): x0 0x42000205 x1 1;
 - ring: CP_SET_SECURE_MODE 0 (0x70e60001 0), flushed and idled, then a
   CP_MEM_WRITE 0xcafef00d check.
SMCs as 0134 (SMC64 SIP standard calls, INTERRUPTED resumed with x0 = 1 and
TZ's x6) plus V2_EBUSY retries; every rc, x1 and resume count is logged.
Fallback only with bluegpu_secvid=1 and no zap: RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL
(0xF400) = 0 by the CPU (may be XPU-protected; not read).

Draw stage diagnostic: RB perf counters (2D_ALIVE_CYCLES, 2D_VALID_PIXELS,
2D_OUTPUT_RB_DST_TRANS, C_WRITE) and CP counter 0 around each fill, and
RBBM_STATUS/1..3 with the A2D/CCU/RB/VBIF busy bits, so "the blit never
ran" and "it ran, the writes went elsewhere" read differently.

Also: the draw stage's framebuffer check mappings come from
ml_io_map_unmappable, the mapping ml_io_unmap can free (ml_io_map's are
permanent io_submap entries).

Boot-args: bluegpu_zap=0|1|2 (default 1 at bluegpu=7: load; 2: only
set_remote_state(0, 13), the a5xx zap resume), bluegpu_secvid=1.
---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/blueline_gpu.c b/bsd/dev/blueline_gpu.c
--- a/bsd/dev/blueline_gpu.c	2026-11-19 10:13:28
+++ b/bsd/dev/blueline_gpu.c	2026-11-19 10:16:20
@@ -10,7 +10,8 @@
  * bluegpu=4 runs stage 1, then 2a with stage 2b (SMMU context + HFI) around it;
  * bluegpu=5 runs 4 with stage 3 (GX: the GPU core powered by the GMU) inside;
  * bluegpu=6 runs 5 with stage 4 (SQE microcode, ringbuffer, first commands) inside 3;
- * bluegpu=7 runs 6, then the draw stage (2D engine fills: own buffer, then the panel);
+ * bluegpu=7 runs 6, then the zap shader (bluegpu_zap, default 1; 0144) and the draw
+ *  stage (2D engine fills: own buffer, then the panel);
  * bluegpu_keep=1 leaves CX and the GMU clocks (and, at 3/4, the running GMU,
  * at 4 also its SMMU bank and memory, at 5 also GX and the votes) on afterwards.
  *
@@ -231,6 +232,62 @@
  *  Down: both mappings cleared from the page tables and cb0's TLB
  *  invalidated before anything else, whatever happened; our buffer is
  *  freed with the CP memory (same conditions), the framebuffer never.
+ *  Diagnostic (0144): RB perf counters around each fill (RB_PERFCTR_RB_SEL
+ *  0..3 = 2D_ALIVE_CYCLES 23, 2D_VALID_PIXELS 28, 2D_OUTPUT_RB_DST_TRANS
+ *  40, C_WRITE 15; RBBM_PERFCTR_RB_0..3 at 0x4d6) with CP counter 0
+ *  (ALWAYS_COUNT) as a check that counters run, and RBBM_STATUS/1..3 with
+ *  the A2D/CCU/RB/VBIF busy bits: 2D counters at 0 mean the blit never ran,
+ *  pixels counted with nothing in memory mean the writes went elsewhere.
+ *
+ * Zap shader (0144, bluegpu=7, bluegpu_zap=1 by default there): between
+ * stage 4's WHERE_AM_I and the draw stage, the GPU leaves secure mode as
+ * mainline a6xx hw_init does after a6xx_cp_init: a6xx_zap_shader_init ->
+ * adreno_zap_shader_load -> zap_shader_load_mdt (qcom_mdt_load into the
+ * zap-shader memory-region, then qcom_pas_auth_and_reset(13)), then
+ * CP_SET_SECURE_MODE 0 in the ring, flushed and idled.
+ *  Image: /blueline-gpu "zap-elf" (tools/mkadt.py --gpu-fw: the phone's
+ *  /vendor/firmware a630_zap.mdt + .b00-.b02 squashed into one ELF as
+ *  pil-squasher does, the same bytes as the vendor's a630_zap.elf; Google
+ *  signed for blueline, never committed). Checked as mdt_header_valid;
+ *  metadata built as qcom_mdt_read_metadata (ELF header + phdrs = phdr[0]
+ *  p_filesz, then the hash segment, the first phdr with (p_flags >> 24) &
+ *  7 == 2, from its p_offset); loadable = PT_LOAD, not hash, p_memsz != 0
+ *  (mdt_phdr_loadable); relocatable if any has bit 27; size =
+ *  ALIGN(max(p_paddr + p_memsz), 4K) - min(p_paddr) (qcom_mdt_get_size).
+ *  This image: one loadable segment (p_paddr 0x5000, 0x7b0 bytes,
+ *  relocatable), hash 0x1988 bytes, metadata 6684 bytes, size 0x1000.
+ *  Region: zap-shader memory-region = gpu_mem 0x8c415000 size 0x2000
+ *  (mainline sdm845.dtsi gpu@8c415000; crosshatch pil_gpu_mem; the
+ *  phone's own carve-out list, LOG.md), below XNU's RAM (0xf4000000+,
+ *  tools/mkadt.py), so never XNU memory. Mapped Device (ml_io_map: no
+ *  speculative reads into a range TZ is about to XPU-lock, and the 16K
+ *  page also covers the ipa_gsi tail), written and read back as words,
+ *  then never touched again; the mapping is left in place.
+ *  PAS (qcom_scm.c, SMC64 SIP standard calls as 0134; INTERRUPTED resumed
+ *  with x0 = 1 and TZ's x6, EBUSY retried 20 x 30 ms; each rc and x1 and
+ *  the resume count logged; Linux's result is rc ? rc : x1):
+ *   is_call_available(PIL, AUTH_AND_RESET) (qcom_pas_is_available);
+ *   INIT_IMAGE x0 0x42000201 x1 0x82 x2 13 x3 meta_pa, the metadata in a
+ *   fresh physically contiguous page below 4G made Normal NC
+ *   (dma_alloc_coherent "non-cachable to avoid XPU violations"; Linux
+ *   frees it after the call, this leaks it);
+ *   MEM_SETUP x0 0x42000202 x1 3 x2 13 x3 0x8c415000 x4 size (relocatable
+ *   images only, as __qcom_mdt_pas_init);
+ *   segments copied to region + p_paddr - min(p_paddr), tails zeroed
+ *   (qcom_mdt_load_no_init), dsb;
+ *   AUTH_AND_RESET x0 0x42000205 x1 1 x2 13 (GX on, CP running, as
+ *   mainline). -4 (EOPNOTSUPP) = no zap on this target.
+ *  Then ring: CP_SET_SECURE_MODE (0x66) 0, submitted and idled, and a
+ *  CP_MEM_WRITE 0xcafef00d to target + 0x40 to check the CP still writes.
+ *  bluegpu_zap=2 instead asks TZ to resume a zap it already holds
+ *  (BOOT set_remote_state(0 = SCM_GPU_ZAP_SHADER_RESUME, 13), as a5xx's
+ *  zap resume; only meaningful after a GPU restart in the same boot).
+ *  bluegpu_zap=0: none. Fallback only if the zap was not authenticated and
+ *  bluegpu_secvid=1: RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL (0xF400) = 0 by the CPU, as
+ *  Linux does when the DT has no zap node; on a zap-required part it may
+ *  be XPU-protected (Linux: "a permissions violation will soon follow"),
+ *  so it is not read before or after. Nothing here can be undone: the zap
+ *  stays authenticated until the next reset; PAS shutdown is never called.
  *
  * Sources (copies and SHAs in pixel3-ios-gpu/ref):
  *  - Linux 20eef29b: sdm845.dtsi (gpu@5000000, gmu@506a000 "gmu" 0x30000,
@@ -327,6 +384,7 @@
 
 extern vm_offset_t ml_io_map(vm_offset_t, vm_size_t);
 extern void ml_io_unmap(vm_offset_t, vm_size_t);	/* osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c */
+extern vm_offset_t ml_io_map_unmappable(vm_offset_t, vm_size_t, uint32_t);	/* the mapping ml_io_unmap frees */
 extern uint32_t blueline_cmddb_addr(const char *id);	/* blueline_touch.c */
 extern uint32_t blueline_cmddb_aux(const char *id, uint8_t *buf, uint32_t max);
 extern bool blueline_cmddb_name(uint32_t addr, char name[9]);
@@ -2242,7 +2300,7 @@
 		cp.sidmask = 0;
 	}
 	printf("BLUELINE GPU: stage 4: CP bring-up (step %d, wait %d ms, sw reset on hang %d, stream 0 mask %#x);"
-	    " no zap, RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL never touched\n", cp.step, cp.ms, cp.reset, cp.sidmask);
+	    " zap (bluegpu_zap) only at bluegpu=7, after WHERE_AM_I\n", cp.step, cp.ms, cp.reset, cp.sidmask);
 	if (SecureDTLookupEntry(NULL, "/blueline-gpu", &node) != kSuccess ||
 	    SecureDTGetProperty(node, "sqe-firmware", &fw, &size) != kSuccess) {
 		printf("BLUELINE GPU: no /blueline-gpu sqe-firmware in the device tree (tools/mkadt.py --gpu-fw with"
@@ -2572,7 +2630,454 @@
 		delay(10);
 		v = cp_mem(off)[0];
 	}
+	return v;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Zap shader (0144): see the top of the file. Linux 20eef29b
+ * drivers/soc/qcom/mdt_loader.c, drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c,
+ * qcom_scm-smc.c, drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.c
+ * (zap_shader_load_mdt), a6xx_gpu.c (hw_init, a6xx_zap_shader_init).
+ */
+#define ZAP_PAS_ID		13u		/* a6xx_gpu.c GPU_PAS_ID; crosshatch qcom,pas-id = <13> */
+#define ZAP_REGION_PA		0x8c415000u	/* sdm845.dtsi gpu_mem / crosshatch pil_gpu_mem */
+#define ZAP_REGION_SIZE		0x2000u
+#define ZAP_META_MAX		0x4000u
+#define ZAP_FILE_MAX		0x10000u
+#define ZAP_CHECK_OFF		(CP_TARGET_OFF + 0x40u)	/* below the draw fences at +0x100 */
+#define ZAP_MEM_WRITE_VAL	0xcafef00du
+#define CP_SET_SECURE_MODE	0x66u
+#define GXR_RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL 0xf400u
+
+#define ELF_PT_LOAD		1u
+#define MDT_TYPE_MASK		(7u << 24)	/* QCOM_MDT_TYPE_MASK */
+#define MDT_TYPE_HASH		(2u << 24)
+#define MDT_RELOCATABLE		(1u << 27)
+
+/* SMCCC / qcom_scm.h */
+#define ZSCM_SMC64		(1u << 30)
+#define ZSCM_OWNER_SIP		(2u << 24)
+#define ZSCM_FNID(svc, cmd)	((((uint32_t)(svc) & 0xffu) << 8) | ((uint32_t)(cmd) & 0xffu))
+#define ZSCM_INTERRUPTED	1
+#define ZSCM_V2_EBUSY		(-12)
+#define ZSCM_MAX_RESUMES	1000u
+#define ZSCM_EBUSY_RETRIES	20u		/* QCOM_SCM_EBUSY_MAX_RETRY, 30 ms apart */
+#define ZSCM_GAVE_UP		(-1000)
+#define ZSCM_SVC_BOOT		0x01u
+#define ZSCM_SVC_PIL		0x02u
+#define ZSCM_SVC_INFO		0x06u
+#define ZSCM_BOOT_SET_REMOTE_STATE 0x0au
+#define ZSCM_PIL_INIT_IMAGE	0x01u
+#define ZSCM_PIL_MEM_SETUP	0x02u
+#define ZSCM_PIL_AUTH_AND_RESET	0x05u
+#define ZSCM_INFO_IS_CALL_AVAIL	0x01u
+#define ZSCM_ARGS_VAL_RW	0x82u		/* QCOM_SCM_ARGS(2, QCOM_SCM_VAL, QCOM_SCM_RW) */
+
+struct zap_phdr {	/* elf32_phdr */
+	uint32_t type, offset, vaddr, paddr, filesz, memsz, flags, align;
+};
+
+static struct {
+	int mode, secvid;
+	const uint8_t *elf;
+	uint32_t size, phoff, phnum;
+	uint32_t ehdr_size, hash_off, hash_size;	/* metadata = elf[0, ehdr_size) + elf[hash_off, + hash_size) */
+	uint32_t min, max;				/* loadable p_paddr span, max 4K aligned */
+	bool relocate, ok, loaded;
+} zap;
+
+static struct zap_phdr
+zap_ph(uint32_t i)
+{
+	struct zap_phdr p;
+	memcpy(&p, zap.elf + zap.phoff + i * sizeof(p), sizeof(p));
+	return p;
+}
+
+static uint32_t
+zap_u32(uint32_t off)
+{
+	uint32_t v;
+	memcpy(&v, zap.elf + off, 4);
 	return v;
+}
+
+static uint16_t
+zap_u16(uint32_t off)
+{
+	uint16_t v;
+	memcpy(&v, zap.elf + off, 2);
+	return v;
+}
+
+/* mdt_phdr_loadable */
+static bool
+zap_loadable(const struct zap_phdr *p)
+{
+	return p->type == ELF_PT_LOAD && (p->flags & MDT_TYPE_MASK) != MDT_TYPE_HASH && p->memsz != 0;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Options and the image (reads only). The checks are mdt_header_valid,
+ * qcom_mdt_read_metadata, qcom_mdt_get_size and qcom_mdt_load_no_init's,
+ * all done here so nothing is sent to TZ for an image Linux would refuse.
+ */
+static void
+zap_prepare(void)
+{
+	DTEntry node;
+	void const *p;
+	unsigned size;
+
+	bzero(&zap, sizeof(zap));
+	zap.mode = 1;
+	(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("bluegpu_zap", &zap.mode, sizeof(zap.mode));
+	(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("bluegpu_secvid", &zap.secvid, sizeof(zap.secvid));
+	if (zap.mode < 0 || zap.mode > 2) {
+		zap.mode = 1;
+	}
+	printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: bluegpu_zap=%d (%s), bluegpu_secvid=%d (RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL fallback %s)\n", zap.mode,
+	    zap.mode == 1 ? "load PAS 13 after WHERE_AM_I" : zap.mode == 2 ? "resume only: set_remote_state(0, 13)" : "off",
+	    zap.secvid, zap.secvid ? "ARMED if the zap fails" : "off");
+	if (zap.mode != 1) {
+		return;
+	}
+	if (SecureDTLookupEntry(NULL, "/blueline-gpu", &node) != kSuccess ||
+	    SecureDTGetProperty(node, "zap-elf", &p, &size) != kSuccess) {
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: no /blueline-gpu zap-elf in the device tree (tools/mkadt.py --gpu-fw with"
+		    " work/fw/vendor/a630_zap.mdt + .b0N): no zap\n");
+		return;
+	}
+	zap.elf = p;
+	zap.size = size;
+	uint32_t sum = 0;
+	for (unsigned i = 0; i + 4 <= size; i += 4) {
+		sum += zap_u32(i);
+	}
+	if (size < 52 || size > ZAP_FILE_MAX || memcmp(zap.elf, "\177ELF", 4) || zap.elf[4] != 1) {
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap-elf %u bytes, word sum %#x: not a 32-bit ELF: no zap\n", size, sum);
+		return;
+	}
+	zap.phoff = zap_u32(0x1c);
+	zap.phnum = zap_u16(0x2c);
+	uint32_t entry = zap_u32(0x18), phentsize = zap_u16(0x2a), shentsize = zap_u16(0x2e), shnum = zap_u16(0x30);
+	printf("BLUELINE GPU: ADT zap-elf %u bytes, word sum %#x, entry %#x, %u phdrs at %#x\n", size, sum, entry, zap.phnum,
+	    zap.phoff);
+	/* mdt_header_valid (section headers: none expected; refused if present, the file is ours to check) */
+	if (phentsize != sizeof(struct zap_phdr) || zap.phnum < 2 || zap.phnum > 64 ||
+	    zap.phoff + zap.phnum * sizeof(struct zap_phdr) > size || shentsize || shnum) {
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap-elf header not valid (phentsize %u, shentsize %u shnum %u): no zap\n", phentsize,
+		    shentsize, shnum);
+		return;
+	}
+	int hash = -1;
+	zap.min = 0xffffffffu;
+	zap.max = 0;
+	for (uint32_t i = 0; i < zap.phnum; i++) {
+		struct zap_phdr h = zap_ph(i);
+		bool ld = zap_loadable(&h);
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap ph%u type %u off %#x paddr %#x filesz %#x memsz %#x flags %#x%s%s\n", i, h.type,
+		    h.offset, h.paddr, h.filesz, h.memsz, h.flags, ld ? " LOAD" : "",
+		    (h.flags & MDT_TYPE_MASK) == MDT_TYPE_HASH ? " HASH" : "");
+		if (i >= 1 && hash < 0 && (h.flags & MDT_TYPE_MASK) == MDT_TYPE_HASH) {
+			hash = (int)i;
+		}
+		if (!ld) {
+			continue;
+		}
+		zap.relocate |= (h.flags & MDT_RELOCATABLE) != 0;
+		if ((uint64_t)h.paddr + h.memsz > 0xffffffffull - 0xfffu || h.filesz > h.memsz ||
+		    (uint64_t)h.offset + h.filesz > size) {
+			printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap ph%u: p_filesz > p_memsz, or its bytes are not in the file: no zap\n", i);
+			return;
+		}
+		zap.min = MIN(zap.min, h.paddr);
+		zap.max = MAX(zap.max, (h.paddr + h.memsz + 0xfffu) & ~0xfffu);
+	}
+	struct zap_phdr h0 = zap_ph(0);
+	if (h0.type == ELF_PT_LOAD || hash < 0 || zap.max <= zap.min) {
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: phdr 0 is PT_LOAD, or no hash segment, or nothing to load: no zap\n");
+		return;
+	}
+	struct zap_phdr hh = zap_ph((uint32_t)hash);
+	zap.ehdr_size = h0.filesz;
+	zap.hash_size = hh.filesz;
+	/* qcom_mdt_read_metadata: the hash follows the header in a bare .mdt, else it is at its p_offset */
+	zap.hash_off = zap.ehdr_size + zap.hash_size == size ? zap.ehdr_size : hh.offset;
+	uint32_t meta = zap.ehdr_size + zap.hash_size, need = zap.max - zap.min;
+	if (zap.ehdr_size < zap.phoff + zap.phnum * sizeof(struct zap_phdr) || zap.hash_off + zap.hash_size > size ||
+	    meta > ZAP_META_MAX || need > ZAP_REGION_SIZE) {
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: header %#x + hash %#x at %#x (metadata max %#x), image %#x (region %#x):"
+		    " does not fit: no zap\n", zap.ehdr_size, zap.hash_size, zap.hash_off, ZAP_META_MAX, need,
+		    ZAP_REGION_SIZE);
+		return;
+	}
+	printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap image ok: metadata %u bytes (header %#x + hash segment %d, %#x bytes at %#x), load"
+	    " %#x-%#x = %#x bytes, %s; region %#x size %#x\n", meta, zap.ehdr_size, hash, zap.hash_size, zap.hash_off,
+	    zap.min, zap.max, need, zap.relocate ? "relocatable (mem_setup)" : "not relocatable", ZAP_REGION_PA,
+	    ZAP_REGION_SIZE);
+	zap.ok = true;
+}
+
+/*
+ * One SCM standard call, as __scm_smc_call / __scm_smc_do / __scm_smc_do_quirk:
+ * x0 fn id, x1 arginfo, x2..x4 args; INTERRUPTED resumed with x0 = 1, x1..x5
+ * as sent and x6 = TZ's; V2_EBUSY retried. Returns x0 (signed), x1 in *r1.
+ */
+static int64_t
+zap_smc(uint32_t svc, uint32_t cmd, uint64_t arginfo, uint64_t a0, uint64_t a1, uint64_t a2, uint64_t *r1,
+    unsigned *resumes)
+{
+	int64_t rc = ZSCM_GAVE_UP;
+
+	*resumes = 0;
+	*r1 = 0;
+	for (unsigned b = 0; b <= ZSCM_EBUSY_RETRIES; b++) {
+		uint64_t id = ZSCM_SMC64 | ZSCM_OWNER_SIP | ZSCM_FNID(svc, cmd), a6 = 0;
+		rc = ZSCM_GAVE_UP;
+		for (unsigned i = 0; i <= ZSCM_MAX_RESUMES; i++) {
+			register uint64_t x0 __asm__("x0") = id;
+			register uint64_t x1 __asm__("x1") = arginfo;
+			register uint64_t x2 __asm__("x2") = a0;
+			register uint64_t x3 __asm__("x3") = a1;
+			register uint64_t x4 __asm__("x4") = a2;
+			register uint64_t x5 __asm__("x5") = 0;
+			register uint64_t x6 __asm__("x6") = a6;
+			register uint64_t x7 __asm__("x7") = 0;
+			__asm__ volatile ("smc #0"
+			    : "+r"(x0), "+r"(x1), "+r"(x2), "+r"(x3), "+r"(x4), "+r"(x5), "+r"(x6), "+r"(x7)
+			    :
+			    : "x8", "x9", "x10", "x11", "x12", "x13", "x14", "x15", "x16", "x17", "cc", "memory");
+			if (x0 == ZSCM_INTERRUPTED) {
+				id = ZSCM_INTERRUPTED;
+				a6 = x6;
+				(*resumes)++;
+				continue;
+			}
+			*r1 = x1;
+			rc = (int64_t)(int32_t)x0;
+			break;
+		}
+		if (rc != ZSCM_V2_EBUSY) {
+			break;
+		}
+		delay(30000);
+	}
+	return rc;
+}
+
+static const char *
+zap_err(int64_t rc)
+{
+	switch (rc) {
+	case 0: return "ok";
+	case -1: return "ERROR";
+	case -2: return "EINVAL_ARG";
+	case -3: return "EINVAL_ADDR";
+	case -4: return "EOPNOTSUPP";
+	case -5: return "ENOMEM";
+	case ZSCM_V2_EBUSY: return "EBUSY (retries used up)";
+	case ZSCM_GAVE_UP: return "still INTERRUPTED, gave up";
+	default: return "error";
+	}
+}
+
+/* One logged PAS/BOOT call; returns Linux's "ret ? : res.result[0]". */
+static int64_t
+zap_call(const char *what, uint32_t svc, uint32_t cmd, uint64_t arginfo, uint64_t a0, uint64_t a1, uint64_t a2)
+{
+	uint64_t r1, t0 = mach_absolute_time(), ns;
+	unsigned resumes;
+
+	printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: about to SMC %s: x0 %#x x1 %#llx x2 %#llx x3 %#llx x4 %#llx\n", what,
+	    ZSCM_SMC64 | ZSCM_OWNER_SIP | ZSCM_FNID(svc, cmd), (unsigned long long)arginfo, (unsigned long long)a0,
+	    (unsigned long long)a1, (unsigned long long)a2);
+	int64_t rc = zap_smc(svc, cmd, arginfo, a0, a1, a2, &r1, &resumes);
+	absolutetime_to_nanoseconds(mach_absolute_time() - t0, &ns);
+	printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: %s -> rc %lld %s, x1 %#llx, %u resume(s), %llu us\n", what, (long long)rc, zap_err(rc),
+	    (unsigned long long)r1, resumes, ns / 1000);
+	return rc ? rc : (int64_t)(int32_t)r1;
+}
+
+/*
+ * qcom_mdt_load + qcom_pas_auth_and_reset (zap_shader_load_mdt). Returns
+ * whether TZ authenticated the zap. Each step stops the sequence on error;
+ * nothing sent to TZ can be taken back.
+ */
+static bool
+zap_load(void)
+{
+	/* qcom_pas_is_available = is_call_available(PIL, AUTH_AND_RESET) */
+	int64_t rc = zap_call("is_call_available(PIL, AUTH_AND_RESET)", ZSCM_SVC_INFO, ZSCM_INFO_IS_CALL_AVAIL, 1,
+	    ZSCM_FNID(ZSCM_SVC_PIL, ZSCM_PIL_AUTH_AND_RESET) | ZSCM_OWNER_SIP, 0, 0);
+	if (rc != 1) {
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: PAS auth_and_reset %s: no zap\n", rc == 0 ? "not available" : "query failed");
+		return false;
+	}
+
+	/* Metadata: physically contiguous, below 4G, Normal NC; leaked afterwards. */
+	uint32_t meta = zap.ehdr_size + zap.hash_size;
+	vm_size_t msz = round_page(meta);
+	vm_offset_t mva = 0;
+	if (kmem_alloc_contig(kernel_map, &mva, msz, PAGE_MASK, (ppnum_t)(atop_64(0x100000000ull) - 1), 0,
+	    KMA_DATA | KMA_ZERO, VM_KERN_MEMORY_IOKIT) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: no contiguous page below 4G for the metadata: no zap\n");
+		return false;
+	}
+	uint64_t mpa = ptoa_64(pmap_find_phys(kernel_pmap, (addr64_t)mva));
+	bool contig = mpa != 0 && mpa + msz <= 0x100000000ull;
+	for (vm_size_t o = 0; o < msz; o += PAGE_SIZE) {
+		ppnum_t pn = pmap_find_phys(kernel_pmap, (addr64_t)(mva + o));
+		contig = contig && ptoa_64(pn) == mpa + o;
+		pmap_set_cache_attributes(pn, VM_WIMG_WCOMB);
+	}
+	volatile uint8_t *m = (volatile uint8_t *)mva;
+	for (uint32_t i = 0; i < meta; i++) {
+		m[i] = i < zap.ehdr_size ? zap.elf[i] : zap.elf[zap.hash_off + i - zap.ehdr_size];
+	}
+	__asm__ volatile ("dsb sy" ::: "memory");
+	uint32_t bad = 0;
+	for (uint32_t i = 0; i < meta; i++) {
+		bad += m[i] != (i < zap.ehdr_size ? zap.elf[i] : zap.elf[zap.hash_off + i - zap.ehdr_size]);
+	}
+	printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap metadata va %#lx pa %#llx (%u bytes in %#lx), %s, cache attr %#x, %u bad bytes\n",
+	    (unsigned long)mva, (unsigned long long)mpa, meta, (unsigned long)msz,
+	    contig ? "contiguous, below 4G" : "NOT CONTIGUOUS OR ABOVE 4G",
+	    pmap_cache_attributes(pmap_find_phys(kernel_pmap, (addr64_t)mva)), bad);
+	if (!contig || bad) {
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: metadata buffer unusable (leaked): no zap\n");
+		return false;
+	}
+
+	/* qcom_scm_pas_init_image: x1 QCOM_SCM_ARGS(2, VAL, RW), x2 pas id, x3 metadata pa */
+	rc = zap_call("PAS init_image(13, metadata)", ZSCM_SVC_PIL, ZSCM_PIL_INIT_IMAGE, ZSCM_ARGS_VAL_RW, ZAP_PAS_ID,
+	    mpa, 0);
+	if (rc) {
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: init_image refused (%lld): TZ did not accept the metadata: no zap\n",
+		    (long long)rc);
+		return false;
+	}
+	/* __qcom_mdt_pas_init: mem_setup only for relocatable images */
+	if (zap.relocate) {
+		rc = zap_call("PAS mem_setup(13, region, size)", ZSCM_SVC_PIL, ZSCM_PIL_MEM_SETUP, 3, ZAP_PAS_ID,
+		    ZAP_REGION_PA, zap.max - zap.min);
+		if (rc) {
+			printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: mem_setup refused (%lld): no zap\n", (long long)rc);
+			return false;
+		}
+	}
+
+	/* qcom_mdt_load_no_init: each loadable segment to region + p_paddr - reloc, the tail zeroed */
+	uint32_t reloc = zap.relocate ? zap.min : ZAP_REGION_PA;
+	printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: about to map and write the zap region at %#x (%#x bytes, Device)\n", ZAP_REGION_PA,
+	    zap.max - zap.min);
+	vm_offset_t rg = ml_io_map(ZAP_REGION_PA, ZAP_REGION_SIZE);	/* kept: io mappings are permanent */
+	if (!rg) {
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: region mapping failed: no zap (PAS 13 left initialised)\n");
+		return false;
+	}
+	for (uint32_t i = 0; i < zap.phnum; i++) {
+		struct zap_phdr h = zap_ph(i);
+		if (!zap_loadable(&h)) {
+			continue;
+		}
+		uint32_t off = h.paddr - reloc;
+		if (h.paddr < reloc || off + h.memsz > zap.max - zap.min) {
+			printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap ph%u: segment outside the region: no zap\n", i);
+			return false;
+		}
+		volatile uint32_t *d = (volatile uint32_t *)(rg + off);
+		uint32_t words = (h.memsz + 3) / 4, wbad = 0;
+		for (uint32_t w = 0; w < words; w++) {
+			uint32_t v = 0;
+			for (uint32_t k = 0; k < 4; k++) {
+				uint32_t o = w * 4 + k;
+				v |= (o < h.filesz ? (uint32_t)zap.elf[h.offset + o] : 0u) << (8 * k);
+			}
+			d[w] = v;
+		}
+		__asm__ volatile ("dsb sy" ::: "memory");
+		for (uint32_t w = 0; w < words; w++) {
+			uint32_t v = 0;
+			for (uint32_t k = 0; k < 4; k++) {
+				uint32_t o = w * 4 + k;
+				v |= (o < h.filesz ? (uint32_t)zap.elf[h.offset + o] : 0u) << (8 * k);
+			}
+			wbad += d[w] != v;
+		}
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap ph%u: %#x bytes (+%#x zero) to pa %#x, first word %#x, %u bad words on read-back\n",
+		    i, h.filesz, h.memsz - h.filesz, ZAP_REGION_PA + off, d[0], wbad);
+		if (wbad) {
+			printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: region did not take the image: no zap\n");
+			return false;
+		}
+	}
+	__asm__ volatile ("dsb sy" ::: "memory");
+
+	/* qcom_pas_auth_and_reset(13): GX on, CP running and idle */
+	rc = zap_call("PAS auth_and_reset(13)", ZSCM_SVC_PIL, ZSCM_PIL_AUTH_AND_RESET, 1, ZAP_PAS_ID, 0, 0);
+	if (rc) {
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: auth_and_reset refused (%lld)%s\n", (long long)rc,
+		    rc == -4 ? ": EOPNOTSUPP, Linux takes this as no zap needed on this target" : ": NOT AUTHENTICATED");
+		return false;
+	}
+	printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: TZ AUTHENTICATED THE ZAP SHADER (region %#x now TZ's; never touched again)\n",
+	    ZAP_REGION_PA);
+	return true;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Between WHERE_AM_I and the draw stage, CP idle. Returns false only if the
+ * ring stopped being usable (the draw stage is then skipped).
+ */
+static bool
+zap_stage(void)
+{
+	if (zap.mode == 1 && zap.ok) {
+		zap.loaded = zap_load();
+	} else if (zap.mode == 2) {
+		/* a5xx zap resume: qcom_scm_set_remote_state(SCM_GPU_ZAP_SHADER_RESUME = 0, 13) */
+		zap.loaded = zap_call("BOOT set_remote_state(0 = zap resume, 13)", ZSCM_SVC_BOOT,
+		    ZSCM_BOOT_SET_REMOTE_STATE, 2, 0, ZAP_PAS_ID, 0) == 0;
+	}
+	cp_smmu_faults("after zap");
+	if (zap.loaded) {
+		/* a6xx hw_init: OUT_PKT7(CP_SET_SECURE_MODE, 1); OUT_RING(0); a6xx_flush; a6xx_idle */
+		uint32_t from = cp.wptr;
+		cp_put(pkt7(CP_SET_SECURE_MODE, 1));
+		cp_put(0);
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: about to submit CP_SET_SECURE_MODE 0 (the CP runs the zap shader)\n");
+		if (!cp_submit("CP_SET_SECURE_MODE 0", from)) {
+			printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: CP_SET_SECURE_MODE 0 did not complete: draw stage skipped\n");
+			return false;
+		}
+	} else if (zap.secvid) {
+		/* a6xx hw_init's -ENODEV branch; KGSL adreno_set_unsecured_mode without zap_loaded */
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: not loaded; bluegpu_secvid=1: about to write RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL (%#x) = 0 by the"
+		    " CPU (may be XPU-protected: a violation can reset the phone)\n", GXR_RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL);
+		cp_wr(GXR_RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL, 0);
+		__asm__ volatile ("dsb sy" ::: "memory");
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL written (not read back)\n");
+	} else {
+		printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: not loaded, no fallback (bluegpu_secvid=0): the GPU stays in secure mode\n");
+		return true;
+	}
+	/* The CP still writes memory after the switch (as 4a, a new value, a fresh word). */
+	uint32_t from = cp.wptr;
+	cp_mem(ZAP_CHECK_OFF)[0] = CP_TARGET_FILL;
+	__asm__ volatile ("dsb sy" ::: "memory");
+	cp_put(pkt7(CP_MEM_WRITE, 3));
+	cp_put(CP_VA + ZAP_CHECK_OFF);
+	cp_put(0);
+	cp_put(ZAP_MEM_WRITE_VAL);
+	cp_put(pkt7(CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE, 0));
+	bool sub = cp_submit("CP_MEM_WRITE after secure mode off", from);
+	uint32_t t = cp_mem_wait(ZAP_CHECK_OFF, CP_TARGET_FILL);
+	printf("BLUELINE GPU: zap: CP_MEM_WRITE after the switch: %#x (want %#x): %s; secure mode left by %s\n", t,
+	    ZAP_MEM_WRITE_VAL, t == ZAP_MEM_WRITE_VAL ? "ok" : "NOT WRITTEN",
+	    zap.loaded ? "CP_SET_SECURE_MODE 0 (zap)" : "RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL 0");
+	cp_smmu_faults("after secure mode off");
+	return sub;
 }
 
